# Backend API layer (`src/api/`)

## Purpose

- **HTTP-agnostic logic** in `src/services/` (shared with legacy) and **`src/api/services/`** for v1-specific orchestration when needed.
- **HTTP adapters** only in **`src/api/http/*.http.ts`** (and `registerApiV1Routes.ts`): parse/validate requests, call services, map status + **v1 JSON envelope**.
- **Legacy** route files stay in `src/routes/` and stay thin; they delegate to the same services as v1 where migrated.
- **Catalog (DBV lists + foil map):** **`/api/v1/catalog/*`** in **`dbv-catalog.http.ts`** → **`CatalogService`** only. Handlers do **not** touch **`CardRepository`** / **`FoilCardMapRepository`** directly—those are wired only into **`CatalogService`** in the composition root.

## Documentation (mandatory)

- **Legacy** contract: [API_DOCUMENTATION.md](../../API_DOCUMENTATION.md)
- **v1** contract: [API_V1.md](../../API_V1.md) — sole place for `/api/v1` paths, examples, `{ data, meta, errors }`.
- **Migration progress:** [API_MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md](../../API_MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md)
- **Architecture narrative:** [MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md](../../MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Agent workflow: [.cursor/skills/api-layer-migration/SKILL.md](../../.cursor/skills/api-layer-migration/SKILL.md)

Any change to a **published HTTP contract** must update the right doc(s) in the **same** change.

## Layering (v1 + migrations)

| Layer | Responsibility | Forbidden |
|-------|----------------|-----------|
| **`*.http.ts`** | Routing, validate → **request models**, call **one** service method, v1 envelope | Business rules, direct DB/repository calls, defining request/response types inline as source of truth |
| **Services** | Business logic; **admin-only** work behind **admin-scoped** entry points only used from `/api/v1/admin/...` | `req`/`res`; branching on **client-supplied** admin/role flags |
| **Repositories** | Persistence | HTTP |
| **Request models** | One **file** per body/query/param contract | Ad hoc `req.body` typing in routes only |
| **Response DTOs** | One **file** per public response shape | Anonymous-only public responses in routes |

## Admin namespace

- Elevated operations only under **`/api/v1/admin/...`**.
- No `isAdmin` / `role` / `elevated` in request bodies to select privileged code paths.
- Non-`/admin` routes **must not** call admin-privileged service methods.

## Passwords / hashing

- **Do not** change password hashing, bcrypt cost, or stored credentials as part of API work.
- v1 login uses **`AuthenticationService.authenticateUser`** (same stack as cookie login); JWT is **after** successful verify.

## Security

- Cross-cutting: middleware (Bearer JWT, rate limits, role checks), not duplicated ad hoc in every handler.
- **JWT:** `JWT_SECRET` required when `NODE_ENV=production`. See [MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md](../../MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Testing (mandatory)

- **Unit:** all service + DTO logic; **full** unit coverage per `src/api/http/*.http.ts` (every route + main error branches).
- **Integration:** **≥1** integration test per `*.http.ts` (Supertest + real app wiring).
- Do not commit without relevant tests passing (`npm run test:unit`; integration when routes are user-visible).

## Imports

- **Never** import from `public/` or frontend bundles into `src/api/`.

## Route grouping (`src/api/http/`)

1. `auth.http.ts` — login, logout, me.
2. `dbv-catalog.http.ts` — card catalog reads for DBV.
3. `dbv-support.http.ts` — DBV reference reads (`/dbv/sets`, `/dbv/deck-backgrounds` with session auth).
4. `decks.http.ts` — user decks: list (`GET /decks`, `DeckListService`); create/validate (`DeckWriteService`); single deck read/update/delete and `/decks/:id/full` (`DeckDetailService`, `UpdateDeckRequestBody`); deck cards (`GET`/`POST`/`PUT`/`DELETE /decks/:id/cards`, `DeckCardsService`, `DeckCardsPostBody` / `DeckCardsPutBody`); UI preferences (`/decks/:id/ui-preferences`). Session auth (same `authenticateUser` as other DB deck routes).
5. `collections.http.ts`, `guest-decks.http.ts`, `admin.http.ts` — as migrations land.

Register via **`registerApiV1Routes`** in `registerApiV1Routes.ts`.

## Endpoint hit metrics

- New **`/api/v1/...`** routes added in `*.http.ts` and mounted through **`registerApiV1Routes`** are included in **`enumerateExpressRoutes`** at server startup and get a **`endpoint_hit_counts` row at zero** (plus runtime upsert on first hit). **Removed** Express routes are dropped from the table on the next startup via **`pruneStaleEndpointHitCounts`**. No Flyway INSERT per route—see [`docs/current/ENDPOINT_HIT_METRICS.md`](../../docs/current/ENDPOINT_HIT_METRICS.md) and [`src/metrics/.cursorrules`](../metrics/.cursorrules).
